# EmailJS Configuration
# Get these values from https://www.emailjs.com/
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key_here
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id_here
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id_here
VITE_RECEIVE_EMAIL=your_email@example.com

# Alternative: Formspree Configuration (if not using EmailJS)
# Get this from https://formspree.io/
VITE_FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/your_form_id

# Instructions:
# 1. Create an EmailJS account at https://www.emailjs.com/
# 2. Create an email service (Gmail, Outlook, etc.)
# 3. Create an email template with the following variables:
#    - {{from_name}} or {{name}} - Sender's name
#    - {{from_email}} or {{email}} - Sender's email
#    - {{message}} - Message content
#    - {{reply_to}} - For reply-to functionality
#    - {{report_type}} - For bug reports (bug/feature)
# 4. Copy your Public Key, Service ID, and Template ID here
# 5. Set VITE_RECEIVE_EMAIL to your email address
# 6. If EmailJS strict mode is enabled, keep Formspree configured as fallback
# 7. Rename this file to .env.local

# The contact form and bug report feature will now send emails to your configured email address!
